{{define "handoff_close" -}}
Every reply you send me goes through the minimizer first: write the reply exactly as you mean to send it — in full, at whatever length the turn calls for — to a file, run `endless task report E-{{.spawned_id}} --draft-file <path> --db main`, and send that command's output as your entire message, verbatim. Do NOT pre-summarize the draft; an adversarial editor decides what survives, and `endless task report --raw` prints your draft back unchanged if it cuts too far. You get one appeal per turn. If I type `$FULL`, that one response bypasses the minimizer entirely — it licenses one response, not a sticky mode. Run `endless worktree check` and put anything it prints in your draft — it stays silent when the worktree is clean, so a clean handoff says nothing about git. Flag external state (CI, services) only if it's actually in play.{{if .bg}} You're a background agent — just stop when done; the user reads this with `claude attach`.{{end}}
{{- end}}

{{define "handoff_verify" -}}
Hand me exactly ONE command to verify this — `esu && ./tests/tasks/e-{{.spawned_id}}-verify.sh` — folding this task's own tests into that one suite as a fail-fast check. Do NOT enumerate a manual checklist. Run the project-wide regression (tests, lint, build) yourself and state the result in one line — never as commands for me to run. See `endless guide orchestration`.
{{- end}}

{{define "handoff_nonverify" -}}
This task delivers information, not testable behavior — there is nothing to verify. Do NOT invent a how-to-test, verification steps, or a checklist; point me to the deliverable and stop.
{{- end}}
